--auto-accept <*flag.boolValue> = "false" : run: auto-answer blocking prompts (affirmative) even with a terminal attached, instead of asking the human
--contain <*flag.stringValue> = "" : run the harness inside an extra Landlock boundary (Linux, ABI 9+, or 6+ with --contain-min-abi and the AppArmor socket layer): landlock; unrelated to --sandbox-defaults, which removes guardrails instead of adding one
--contain-allow-tcp <*main.portList> = "" : with --contain-restrict-tcp: allow outbound TCP connects to this port (repeatable)
--contain-min-abi <*flag.intValue> = "0" : with --contain: the lowest Landlock ABI to accept (default 9, minimum 6); below 9 pathname UNIX sockets are denied by the AppArmor socket layer (see contain-apparmor-profile)
--contain-pass-env <*main.stringList> = "" : with --contain: also pass this environment variable to the harness (repeatable; names only)
--contain-restrict-tcp <*flag.boolValue> = "false" : with --contain: deny TCP bind and every TCP connect except to --contain-allow-tcp ports (none listed: deny all TCP)
--contain-ro <*main.stringList> = "" : with --contain: grant read-only access to an existing absolute path (repeatable)
--contain-rw <*main.stringList> = "" : with --contain: grant read-write access to an existing absolute path (repeatable)
--contain-state-dir <*flag.stringValue> = "" : with --contain: keep HOME and harness state in this existing directory (shared, persistent) instead of private per-session state
--effort <*flag.stringValue> = "" : reasoning effort for supported harnesses (low, medium, high, xhigh, max)
--model <*flag.stringValue> = "" : model id for supported harnesses (claude --model, codex -c model)
--permission-mode <*flag.stringValue> = "" : launch-time permission rung for claude/codex: plan, manual, ask, auto, bypass (per-harness native spellings also pass through); bypass does NOT set IS_SANDBOX=1 (acceptance screen appears, root disallowed); combine with --sandbox-defaults for that, or --auto-accept to answer the screen in an interactive run; restrictive rungs bind fully only with a human at the TUI
--sandbox-defaults <*flag.boolValue> = "false" : run/structured-run: claude only — DANGEROUS: inject --dangerously-skip-permissions into harness args and set IS_SANDBOX=1 in the harness env (meta-harness parity; IS_SANDBOX=1 also suppresses the bypass-permissions acceptance screen and allows root); no-op for other harnesses; rejected by the default passthrough mode
--tmux-child <*flag.stringValue> = "" : internal: in-pane re-exec marker; do not set manually
--tmux-session <*flag.stringValue> = "" : spawn the run inside a detached tmux session named hw-<value> and exit immediately
--trace-file <*flag.stringValue> = "" : path to write trace events as NDJSON (default: trace events are dropped)
--trace-stderr <*flag.boolValue> = "false" : write trace events as NDJSON to stderr (mutually exclusive with --trace-file)
